\item RHS \code{ref}: \strong{Required, named, no default}, for every
association regardless of \code{fun}. This is the covariate value (for
continuous covariates) or raw level (for categorical covariates)
that the effect is normalized against -- the point at which the
reported effect ratio is exactly \code{1}. There is no way to safely infer
this from the \code{xpdb} alone (NONMEM control streams commonly
